{"data":{"body":"[P2] Return the untested error guards to the design phase\n\nRule 4, \u201cEvery branch has a test that fails without it,\u201d remains unsatisfied. Both test parametrizations use the helper that raises `HELPER_FAILURE`; neither exercises a different error message or an unexpected successful return. Removing either defensive rejection leaves the test results unchanged. Return to the design phase under rule 8 and decide whether these cases need meaningful coverage or whether the fixed fixture permits a simpler approach.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPsIIsM8AAAABBfLhgA","finding_digest":"81c3ad6427b41fe2f2973d192b6cdf6eff6f114d8404420177a8894effecdb43","finding_id":"arf_v1_qhb22zbhwqp6f4uxhumsw3g7n3","finding_key":"conformance-tests-otel::otel_23_callback_function_context.handler::untested-error-guards","identity_key":"conformance-tests-otel::otel_23_callback_function_context.handler::untested-error-guards","line":130,"observation_digest":"a01901085ec25694830d9558abe44e6612780b06ac5828fc7f395dabb965bb0c","observation_id":"aro_v1_uamqccc6yjljjaynsvmkxzcomy","path":"packages/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python-conformance-tests-otel/src/otel_23_callback_function_context.py","prior_finding_id":"arf_v1_qhb22zbhwqp6f4uxhumsw3g7n3","published_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:45Z","review_id":"arr_v1_s6xvtrl5veafqmuxlq5ozq5czp","reviewed_base_sha":"a8baa73c32904cfd6a1c03155899a3753c954249","reviewed_head_sha":"dc736d5c77f0f8c5be9a15a2d00a2ac47f3e1691","reviewer":"codex","start_line":127,"suggestion_id":""},"pull_request":{"number":796},"record_id":"art_v1_4togihbipi2vwzkyqn567eo2zt","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:45Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python","id":1052903600},"schema_version":1}
